Workers can be allocated to gather the following resources:
* {{plink|Wood (Anachronia base camp)|txt=Wood}}
* {{plink|Vines (Anachronia base camp)|txt=Vines}}
* {{plink|Leaves (Anachronia base camp)|txt=Leaves}}
* {{plink|Hides (Anachronia base camp)|txt=Hides}}
* {{plink|Stone (Anachronia base camp)|txt=Stone}}
* {{plink|Clay (Anachronia base camp)|txt=Clay}}

These resources can be gathered to build and upgrade various structures in the base camp, animal pens on the [[Anachronia Dinosaur Farm]], and skilling stations in [[Dream of Iaia]]. Before building the storehouse, the maximum amount (or cap) of each resource that can be held is 5,000. The storehouse section below details the cap for each tier; up to 150,000 for Tier 3. Workers will continue to gather resources when the player is logged out or not at the base camp. Each worker assigned to a resource will gather 60 of that resource each hour, updating at approximate 10 minute intervals, until the storehouse cap has been hit. The timing of the updates varies with respect to the game time on a world-to-world basis.

[[Compacted resources]] can also be found whilst skilling or killing the local fauna. These can be sent to the base camp to gain 100, 200, or 400 resources with a tier 1, 2, or 3 town hall built respectively.

==Base camp structures==
===Town Hall===
{{Main|Town Hall (Anachronia base camp)}}
The first tier of the Town Hall is made during the base camp introduction in the eastern base camp. [[Mr. Mordaut]], [[Giles]], and [[general store assistant]] can be found here. Upgrading the Town Hall is required to upgrade all other base camp structures. A [[Deposit box (Anachronia base camp)|deposit box]] is located here; a [[Bank chest (Anachronia base camp)|bank chest]] is available as an upgrade. The tier 2 town hall brings with it an [[armour store assistant]] (west of [[Laniakea]]) and a [[weapon store assistant]] (in the storehouse). The tier 3 Town Hall brings with it a [[gem store assistant]] (eastern side of the base camp) and a [[rune store assistant]] (south of the spa).

