==Strategy==
Since the materials for the tier 1 Town Hall are provided during the tutorial, the player needs to focus on gathering resources for other buildings. It is highly recommended that a player builds the Anachronia lodestone, followed by upgrading the deposit box into a bank chest, before anything else in order to allow a central access point to every location on the island and provide the ability to bank on Anachronia.

Once the lodestone and bank chest are accessible, rotate between upgrading the Storehouse, Sleeping Quarters, and Town Hall until they are all tier 3. Doing this will allow the highest amount of storage for resources and the maximum amount of workers for constructing other buildings and nodes around the island, which would otherwise impede growth of the camp. 

There are a couple of strategies when devoting workers to gather resources;

# Assign workers evenly to the required resources, or
# Assign the maximum amount of workers to one resource until the required amount for a building or node has been acquired, then switch to the next resource.

Option 1 is an easier way to gather resources and requires the least amount of input. However, Option 2 can be slightly faster when gathering a specific resource, though it necessitates regular visits to the camp unless you have unlocked the [[Command Centre]] in [[Fort Forinthry]], which allows for remote camp management from the Command Centre.

Overall, it will require a minimum of 880 hours to get the Town Hall, Storehouse, and Sleeping Quarters buildings to tier 3 if gathering resources via workers and not making use of compacted resources. After this, it will take 468.75 hours to get the Spa, Hunter Lodge, and Slayer Lodge structures to tier 3, with an additional 197.5 hours for a tier 3 Player Lodge. As a result, it takes approximately 1,550 hours to construct all tier 3 Base Camp structures, or a minimum of 64 days and 14 hours.

To create tier 3 deposit and bait boxes, the overall time will increase to approximately 1,672 hours, or a minimum of 69 days.

Resource acquisition can be sped up considerably with [[Advance Time]] at level 93 Magic, adding 72 hours each real week. This is 43% faster resource gain, which results in 30% less time taken overall. Alternatively, when skilling in Anachronia, different types of [[Compacted resources]] may be obtained and the player may choose to focus the workers on the resources they may not be able to gather themselves.

While players can acquire the important upgrades to Tier 3 buildings such as the [[dinosaur tooth]], [[dinosaur rib bone]] at the Anachronia Base Camp through random skilling activities, Slayer, or [[Big Game Hunter]], the [[Dream of Iaia]] is likely to drop all the upgrade materials within several days of using the dream because of the very high rate of XP drops within the Dream that allow for a roll on the table.

